      <h1>Lithium Storage and Transport State of Charge — What the Rules Require</h1>
      <div class="takeaways"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> For air transport, lithium cells and batteries are generally limited to about 30% state of charge. For long-term storage, a partial charge — not full, not empty — slows aging. The BMS should be put to sleep, and the state of charge should be documented.</div>

<h2>Transport: why 30%</h2>
<p>A lithium cell at high state of charge holds more energy and is more reactive if it fails. The air-transport rules therefore limit the state of charge for cells and batteries shipped alone (not in equipment) to about 30% of rated capacity. The exact limit and the exceptions depend on the mode and the packing instruction; confirm the current edition with the carrier.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Typical SOC rule</th><th>Documentation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Air (cells/batteries alone)</td><td>≤30% SOC</td><td>UN38.3 summary, declaration, SOC statement</td></tr>
<tr><td>Air (in equipment)</td><td>Equipment-specific; often ≤30% or disabled</td><td>Declaration, packing instruction</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sea / road</td><td>Mode and carrier rules apply</td><td>Dangerous goods documentation</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Long-term storage</h2>
<p>Store at 30–50% state of charge, in a cool, dry place, away from flammable material. A full pack ages faster; an empty pack can drift into over-discharge. Check the voltage periodically and recharge if it falls below the manufacturer's minimum.</p>
<h2>BMS sleep and self-consumption</h2>
<p>A BMS left awake draws a small current that can flatten a pack over months. Use the sleep or shipping mode, disconnect the load, and record the state of charge at the start of storage. A pack that arrives at 0 V after a year in a warehouse has probably been over-discharged.</p>
<h2>What to ask a supplier</h2>
<ol><li>At what state of charge will the pack ship, and how is it verified?</li><li>Is the BMS in shipping mode, and what is the self-consumption?</li><li>What is the maximum storage temperature and the recommended recharge interval?</li><li>Does the documentation include the SOC statement the carrier requires?</li></ol>

